From 5c7c79cd01a9799cc95fca55b6cdbff899229d87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:43:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] feat(ui): edit a tool in the tool library window

A tool opens in the tool library window's own editor. The list folds
into a rail; the editor has a Tool tab (the geometry and kind rows of
Properties) and a Details tab (material group, catalog facts, tool
number). Apply queues ChangeTool (and SetToolNumber when the number
changed), so a geometry and catalog edit is one undo step.

The window keeps its own draft in ToolLibraryView::editor and swaps it
into tool_ui only while it draws and applies, so Properties and the
window can show two tools without a mix of drafts.

Fixes #3893

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
